<title>USA: OLYMPUS U.S. UNIT SAYS REACHES SETTLEMENT.</title>
<headline>OLYMPUS U.S. UNIT SAYS REACHES SETTLEMENT.</headline>
<dateline>MELVILLE, N.Y. 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Olympus Optical Co Ltd's Olympus America Inc said Thursday it agreed to pay the U.S. government $22.8 million to settle a dispute with the Department of Veterans Affairs.</p>
<p>The U.S. subsidiary of the Japanese company said its results for fiscal 1997, which ends March 31, already reflected the $22.8 million charge.</p>
<p>A spokesman declined to disclose details of the dispute with the Department of Veterans. The company said the settlement was not an admission of wrongdoing or liability.</p>
</text>
